Try Earth's atmospheric glow in an isolated globe render
======================================================

The Rayleigh effect is drawn on the spherical globe, not on a projected
world map such as Lambert. Omit the -projection option. The shipped
earthRayleigh file is a recipe, not a set of lookup tables.

From a new scratch directory, copy the installed earthRayleigh file
into a scattering subdirectory and generate the tables there:

    mkdir scattering
    cp /path/to/share/xplanet/scattering/earthRayleigh scattering/
    (cd scattering && xplanet -create_scattering_tables ./earthRayleigh)

This takes a few minutes and writes the tables to the current directory.
Keep the recipe and tables together. Create atmosphere.conf:

    [earth]
    rayleigh_file=earthRayleigh
    rayleigh_scale=10
    rayleigh_limb_scale=4

Render an off-center sunlit globe to see the effect:

    xplanet -searchdir "$PWD" -config "$PWD/atmosphere.conf" \
      -target earth -date 20260320.120000 -longitude 115 -latitude 0 \
      -geometry 1200x720 -radius 75 -starfreq 0 \
      -num_times 1 -output atmosphere.png

To compare, repeat with a config containing only [earth]. The limb scale of 4
exaggerates the atmosphere to show it at preview size; 1 is the default.
This writes a file only and does not change an existing wallpaper.
